    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0746" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Greece/100</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Greek Minister (Simopoulos) to the Acting
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-12">May 12, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Greece presents his compliments to His Excellency the Acting
                    Secretary of State and, referring to his note of May 4, 1932,<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d426-f1"/> and to his conversations with officials of the Department
                    of State and Treasury Department, has the honor to inform him that it is
                    understood that if, after the signature by Greece of the agreement concerning
                    the postponement of payments due during the fiscal year of 1936 and their
                    repayment over a 10 year period, more favorable terms should have been granted
                    to other governments, included in the Joint Resolution of Congress approved
                    December 23, 1931, these should be extended also to the Greek Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
